{
  "id": "exponent-rules",
  "title": "Exponent Rules",
  "description": "The product, quotient, and power rules for exponents, plus zero and negative exponents, and problems that mix them. (\"Quotient rule\" here is the exponent rule, not the calculus one.)",
  "strand": "algebra",
  "status": "starter",
  "reference": {
    "title": "Exponent rules (from class)",
    "rows": [
      { "label": "Product rule", "rule": "x<sup>a</sup> · x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a+b</sup>" },
      { "label": "Quotient rule", "rule": "x<sup>a</sup> / x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup>" },
      { "label": "Power rule", "rule": "(x<sup>a</sup>)<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a·b</sup>" },
      { "label": "Zero exponent", "rule": "x<sup>0</sup> = 1", "note": "x ≠ 0" },
      { "label": "Negative exponent", "rule": "x<sup>−a</sup> = 1/x<sup>a</sup>" }
    ],
    "foot": "Same base x in each rule. Multiply → add exponents. Divide → subtract. Power of a power → multiply."
  },
  "practice": [
    {
      "id": "exp-p01",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Product rule: x³ · x⁵ = xⁿ. What is n?",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three x tiles labeled x cubed, times five x tiles labeled x to the 5th, equals x to the n.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [{ "n": 3, "text": "x", "label": "x³" }, { "n": 5, "text": "x", "label": "x⁵" }],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "xⁿ",
          "caption": "n = ?"
        }
      },
      "answer": "8",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "3 + 5",
      "hints": [
        "Product rule: x<sup>a</sup> · x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a+b</sup>. Same base, multiplying → <b>add</b> the exponents.",
        "Count the tiles: 3 x's times 5 more x's.",
        "3 + 5 = ?"
      ],
      "solution": "x³ · x⁵ = x³⁺⁵ = x⁸, so n = <b>8</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p02",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Evaluate 2³ · 2².",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three tiles of 2 labeled 2 cubed, times two tiles of 2 labeled 2 squared.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [{ "n": 3, "text": "2", "label": "2³" }, { "n": 2, "text": "2", "label": "2²" }],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "?"
        }
      },
      "answer": "32",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "2**3 * 2**2",
      "hints": ["Same base 2, multiplying → add the exponents.", "2³ · 2² = 2⁵.", "2⁵ = 2 · 2 · 2 · 2 · 2."],
      "solution": "2³ · 2² = 2³⁺² = 2⁵ = <b>32</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p03",
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Simplify (3x⁴)(5x²).",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "The terms 3 x to the 4th and 5 x squared written as tiles: 3, x, x, x, x times 5, x, x.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "items": ["3", "x", "x", "x", "x"], "label": "3x⁴" },
            { "items": ["5", "x", "x"], "label": "5x²" }
          ],
          "sep": "·"
        }
      },
      "choices": ["15x⁶", "8x⁶", "15x⁸", "8x⁸"],
      "answer": "15x⁶",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": [
        "Multiply the numbers in front (the coefficients).",
        "3 · 5 = 15.",
        "For the x's, use the product rule: add the exponents, 4 + 2."
      ],
      "solution": "(3 · 5)(x⁴ · x²) = 15x⁴⁺² = <b>15x⁶</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p04",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Quotient rule: x⁹ / x⁴ = xⁿ. What is n?",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Nine x tiles over four x tiles, equals x to the n.",
        "chips": { "num": { "n": 9, "text": "x" }, "den": { "n": 4, "text": "x" }, "rhs": "xⁿ", "caption": "n = ?" }
      },
      "answer": "5",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "9 - 4",
      "hints": [
        "Quotient rule: x<sup>a</sup> / x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup>. Same base, dividing → <b>subtract</b> the exponents.",
        "Each x on the bottom cancels one x on top.",
        "9 − 4 = ?"
      ],
      "solution": "x⁹ / x⁴ = x⁹⁻⁴ = x⁵, so n = <b>5</b> (four pairs cancel, five x's are left)"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p05",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Evaluate 5⁷ / 5⁵.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Seven tiles of 5 over five tiles of 5.",
        "chips": { "num": { "n": 7, "text": "5" }, "den": { "n": 5, "text": "5" }, "rhs": "?" }
      },
      "answer": "25",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "5**7 / 5**5",
      "hints": ["Same base, dividing → subtract the exponents.", "7 − 5 = 2, so the result is 5².", "5² = 25."],
      "solution": "5⁷ / 5⁵ = 5⁷⁻⁵ = 5² = <b>25</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p06",
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Simplify (12x⁷y³) / (4x²y⁵). Use only positive exponents.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "The fraction 12 x to the 7th y cubed over 4 x squared y to the 5th.",
        "frac": { "num": "12x⁷y³", "den": "4x²y⁵", "rhs": "?" }
      },
      "choices": ["3x⁵/y²", "3x⁵y²", "8x⁵/y²", "3x⁹/y⁸"],
      "answer": "3x⁵/y²",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": [
        "Work in three parts: the numbers, the x's, and the y's.",
        "12 ÷ 4 = 3, and x⁷ / x² = x⁵.",
        "y³ / y⁵ = y⁻² = 1/y²."
      ],
      "solution": "12 ÷ 4 = 3<br>x⁷⁻² = x⁵<br>y³⁻⁵ = y⁻² = 1/y²<br>Answer: <b>3x⁵/y²</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p07",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Power rule: (x²)³ = xⁿ. What is n?",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three groups, each two x tiles labeled x squared, multiplied together. Equals x to the n.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" }
          ],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "xⁿ",
          "caption": "(x²)³ means x² three times; n = ?"
        }
      },
      "answer": "6",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "2 * 3",
      "hints": [
        "Power rule: (x<sup>a</sup>)<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a·b</sup>. A power of a power → <b>multiply</b> the exponents.",
        "(x²)³ = x² · x² · x².",
        "2 · 3 = ?"
      ],
      "solution": "(x²)³ = x²·³ = x⁶, so n = <b>6</b> (three groups of two x's)"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p08",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Evaluate (2²)³.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three groups, each two tiles of 2, labeled 2 squared.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "n": 2, "text": "2", "label": "2²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "2", "label": "2²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "2", "label": "2²" }
          ],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "?"
        }
      },
      "answer": "64",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "(2**2)**3",
      "hints": ["Power rule: multiply the exponents.", "(2²)³ = 2⁶.", "2⁶ = 64. (Check: 2² = 4, and 4³ = 64.)"],
      "solution": "(2²)³ = 2²·³ = 2⁶ = <b>64</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p09",
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Simplify (2x³)².",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Two groups, each with tiles 2, x, x, x, labeled 2 x cubed.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "items": ["2", "x", "x", "x"], "label": "2x³" },
            { "items": ["2", "x", "x", "x"], "label": "2x³" }
          ],
          "sep": "·"
        }
      },
      "choices": ["4x⁶", "2x⁶", "4x⁵", "2x⁹"],
      "answer": "4x⁶",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": [
        "The power goes on <b>everything</b> inside the parentheses: the 2 and the x³.",
        "2² = 4.",
        "(x³)² = x³·² by the power rule."
      ],
      "solution": "(2x³)² = 2² · (x³)² = 4 · x⁶ = <b>4x⁶</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p10",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Evaluate 5x⁰ when x = 8.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three x tiles over three x tiles: every tile cancels.",
        "chips": {
          "num": { "n": 3, "text": "x" },
          "den": { "n": 3, "text": "x" },
          "rhs": "x⁰",
          "ask": false,
          "caption": "why x⁰ = 1"
        }
      },
      "answer": "5",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "5 * 8**0",
      "hints": [
        "Zero exponent: x⁰ = 1 for any x ≠ 0. (x³ / x³ = x⁰, and anything over itself is 1.)",
        "The exponent 0 is only on the x, not on the 5.",
        "5 · 1 = ?"
      ],
      "solution": "x⁰ = 1, so 5x⁰ = 5 · 1 = <b>5</b>. (Careful: (5x)⁰ would be 1.)"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p11",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Evaluate 2⁻³. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Two tiles of 2 over five tiles of 2. After canceling, three 2s are left on the bottom.",
        "chips": {
          "num": { "n": 2, "text": "2" },
          "den": { "n": 5, "text": "2" },
          "rhs": "2⁻³",
          "ask": false,
          "caption": "one way to get 2⁻³"
        }
      },
      "answer": "1/8",
      "acceptable": ["0.125"],
      "check": "2**-3",
      "hints": [
        "Negative exponent: x<sup>−a</sup> = 1/x<sup>a</sup>. It means \"one over\", not a negative number.",
        "2⁻³ = 1/2³.",
        "2³ = 8."
      ],
      "solution": "2⁻³ = 1/2³ = <b>1/8</b> (0.125)"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p12",
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Rewrite 3x⁻² using only positive exponents.",
      "figure": { "alt": "The expression 3 times x to the negative 2.", "frac": { "num": "3 · x⁻²", "den": "1", "rhs": "?" } },
      "choices": ["3/x²", "1/(3x²)", "−3x²", "9/x²"],
      "answer": "3/x²",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": ["The −2 exponent belongs only to x, not to the 3.", "x⁻² = 1/x².", "3 · 1/x² = ?"],
      "solution": "3x⁻² = 3 · 1/x² = <b>3/x²</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p13",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Mixed: (x³ · x⁵) / x² = xⁿ. What is n?",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "The fraction x cubed times x to the 5th, over x squared, equals x to the n.",
        "frac": { "num": "x³ · x⁵", "den": "x²", "rhs": "xⁿ", "caption": "n = ?" }
      },
      "answer": "6",
      "acceptable": [],
      "check": "3 + 5 - 2",
      "hints": ["Do the top first with the product rule: x³ · x⁵ = x⁸.", "Then the quotient rule: x⁸ / x².", "8 − 2 = ?"],
      "solution": "Top: x³ · x⁵ = x⁸ (add)<br>Then x⁸ / x² = x⁶ (subtract)<br>n = <b>6</b>"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-p14",
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Mixed: simplify (2x³)² · x.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Two groups of tiles 2, x, x, x, labeled 2 x cubed, times one more x tile.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "items": ["2", "x", "x", "x"], "label": "2x³" },
            { "items": ["2", "x", "x", "x"], "label": "2x³" },
            { "n": 1, "text": "x", "label": "x" }
          ],
          "sep": "·"
        }
      },
      "choices": ["4x⁷", "4x⁶", "2x⁷", "4x¹⁰"],
      "answer": "4x⁷",
      "acceptable": [],
      "hints": ["Power rule first: (2x³)² = 4x⁶.", "Then the product rule: x⁶ · x = x⁶ · x¹.", "6 + 1 = ?"],
      "solution": "(2x³)² = 4x⁶ (power rule)<br>4x⁶ · x¹ = 4x⁷ (product rule)<br>Answer: <b>4x⁷</b>"
    }
  ],
  "flashcards": [
    {
      "id": "exp-fc01",
      "front": "Product rule",
      "back": "x<sup>a</sup> · x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a+b</sup><br>Same base, multiplying → <b>add</b> the exponents. Example: x³ · x⁵ = x⁸.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three x tiles times two x tiles makes five x tiles.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [{ "n": 3, "text": "x", "label": "x³" }, { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" }],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "x⁵",
          "ask": false
        }
      },
      "figureSide": "back"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc02",
      "front": "Quotient rule",
      "back": "x<sup>a</sup> / x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup> (x ≠ 0)<br>Same base, dividing → <b>subtract</b> the exponents. Example: x⁵ / x² = x³.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Five x tiles over two x tiles. Two pairs are crossed out, leaving three x tiles on top.",
        "chips": { "num": { "n": 5, "text": "x" }, "den": { "n": 2, "text": "x" }, "cancel": 2, "rhs": "x³", "ask": false }
      },
      "figureSide": "back"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc03",
      "front": "Power rule",
      "back": "(x<sup>a</sup>)<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a·b</sup><br>Power of a power → <b>multiply</b> the exponents. Example: (x²)³ = x⁶.",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Three groups of two x tiles makes six x tiles.",
        "chips": {
          "groups": [
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" },
            { "n": 2, "text": "x", "label": "x²" }
          ],
          "sep": "·",
          "rhs": "x⁶",
          "ask": false
        }
      },
      "figureSide": "back"
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc04",
      "front": "Zero exponent",
      "back": "x<sup>0</sup> = 1 (x ≠ 0)<br>Reason: x³ / x³ = x⁰, and anything divided by itself is 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc05",
      "front": "Negative exponent",
      "back": "x<sup>−a</sup> = 1/x<sup>a</sup><br>Example: 2⁻³ = 1/8. A negative exponent does <b>not</b> make the number negative."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc06",
      "front": "Negative exponent on the bottom",
      "back": "1/x<sup>−a</sup> = x<sup>a</sup>. Moving a factor across the fraction bar flips the sign of its exponent."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc07",
      "front": "Power of a product",
      "back": "(xy)<sup>a</sup> = x<sup>a</sup>y<sup>a</sup>. The power goes on every factor: (2x³)² = 4x⁶."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc08",
      "front": "Power of a quotient",
      "back": "(x/y)<sup>a</sup> = x<sup>a</sup>/y<sup>a</sup> (y ≠ 0). Example: (2/5)³ = 8/125."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc09",
      "front": "Numbers in front (coefficients)",
      "back": "Multiply or divide the numbers like normal; use the exponent rules only on the variables. (3x⁴)(5x²) = 15x⁶."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc10",
      "front": "Add, subtract, or multiply?",
      "back": "Multiplying powers → add. Dividing powers → subtract. Power of a power → multiply. Common mistakes: x³ · x⁵ is x⁸ (not x¹⁵), and (x²)³ is x⁶ (not x⁵)."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc11",
      "front": "5x⁰ vs (5x)⁰",
      "back": "5x⁰ = 5 · 1 = 5, because the 0 is only on the x. (5x)⁰ = 1, because the 0 is on everything in the parentheses."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc12",
      "front": "\"Quotient rule\": which one?",
      "back": "In calculus, \"quotient rule\" means a rule for derivatives of fractions (f/g)′. That's a different topic. In this class it means the exponent rule x<sup>a</sup>/x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup>."
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-fc13",
      "front": "Looking it up online?",
      "back": "Search for \"exponent rules\" or \"quotient of powers\". A search for just \"quotient rule\" or \"product rule\" often shows the calculus derivative rules, which are not what this unit covers."
    }
  ],
